[
  {
    "sha": "81e4cb015d0ae9e6daf4c549726fcf3001e1359e",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDgxZTRjYjAxNWQwYWU5ZTZkYWY0YzU0OTcyNmZjZjMwMDFlMTM1OWU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T11:54:12Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T11:54:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): the workholding rpm limit judges the work spindle, not a live tool's speed\n\nThe chuck / collet limit (#1031) used spindle_law::turns, which also\ncounts the cross drill (a driven radial tool, the work held still), so\na 10000 rpm cross drill was refused under a 100 rpm chuck with the\nfalse text \"turns the work at 10000 rpm\". The program gate now sorts\neach section by which spindle its S drives, as the lathe post does:\nturning and the lathe's axial drill turn the work at the stated rpm\n(G97 refused above the limit; the G96 clamp unchanged); a C-axis\nlive-tool section (moves state C) turns the work only on C, judged by\nthe machine's C rate (refused by name when that is over the limit or\nunstated while a limit is stated); a cross drill is not judged.\n\nFixes #1174\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
