      "message": "fix(turning): the workholding limit reads the post's own section derivation; no kind fails open\n\nReview of PR #1191: the gate fell back to spindle_law::turns, which\ncounts an on-centre Drill only on a pure lathe, so a mill-turn's\non-centre drill at 8000 rpm posted G97 S8000 M03 under a 2000 rpm chuck.\nThe lathe post opens every section without PARAM LiveTool on the work\nspindle, whatever its kind. post::section_spindle::of(path) is now the\none derivation: post::dump writes PARAM LiveTool and the A/B pose words\nfrom it, and setup_workholding::work_speed reads it - on a lathe or\nmill-turn a Work section is judged at its stated rpm, a LiveTool\nsection by the machine's C rate, a Posed section is the post's refusal.\nlathe_workholding_kinds proves it for every kind a lathe or mill-turn\nadmits.\n\nRefs #1174\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
