      },
      "message": "Merge #1202 (issue/1190-mill-op-on-lathe-post): one dialect reader, one section derivation\n\nThe workholding rule now reads #1190's lathe_voice::voice_of for the\nsection and post::dialect::work_voice (the manifest mask, three ways;\nspeaks_turning reads it too) for the script that runs - the machine kind\nis no part of it except a plain lathe, whose one spindle holds the chuck\n(only widens). post::section_spindle is gone; post::dump writes the\nstream from dialect::states_live_tool as on #1202 (byte-identical).\nUndeclared scripts take the stricter reading (#1199). Refusal text shows\none decimal when whole rpm would print the speed and the limit the same.\n\nRefs #1174\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
