        "date": "2026-11-12T13:35:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): a work-spindle section through a milling post on a mill-turn is held to the chuck\n\nThird review of PR #1191: the milling-post arm of work_speed spared every\nsection on a mill-turn, so a facing op at 3000 rpm under a 2000 rpm chuck\nposted S3000 M3 through fanuc.cps and haas.cps (main refused it). On a\nlathe or mill-turn a work-spindle section only cuts if the work turns, so\nit is judged at its rpm whatever the post calls itself; a mill-turn's\nmilling section through a milling post stays unjudged; a C section on a\nchucked machine is judged by the C rate under any post. Pinned by\nlathe_workholding_mill_post, with a walk over every machine kind x post\ndialect x section.\n\nRefs #1174\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
